*.log
*.sqlite3

# Ignore macOS specific files
.DS_Store

# Ignore Windows specific files
Thumbs.db


simulation_outputs*/
analysis_outputs*/
examples/analysis/*

# ★ THE PARTIAL-PROGRESS FILE IS A CRASH ARTEFACT, NOT A RECORD (L22 decision).
#
# It is rewritten WHOLESALE every timestep, so tracking it means the tree is dirty
# for the whole of every run -- and committing it is what turned a harmless
# overwrite into a committed file describing the wrong episode.
#
# It does its job ON DISK, which is where a recovering process looks. When an
# episode dies WITHOUT a bundle, the partial IS the record: `git add -f` it then,
# with a commit message saying why that one is in the record.
#
# FLIP CONDITION, stated so it is not rediscovered: if we ever run UNATTENDED,
# this inverts -- an untracked file is one `git clean` from gone, and nobody is
# there to force-add it.
experiments/worker_replacement/records/**/partial_*.json
